quran[25]{c,v,t}:
  20,13,"I have chosen you (as My messenger), so listen to what is revealed."
  20,14,"Indeed, I am Allah. There is no god but Me. So worship Me and establish the prayer for My remembrance."
  20,15,"Indeed, the Hour is coming. I would keep it hidden so that every soul may be recompensed for what it strives for."
  20,16,"So let not avert you from it, the one who does not believe in it, and follows his base desires, lest you should perish."
  20,17,"(Allah asked:) ‘What is that in your right hand, O Musa (Moses)?’"
  20,18,"He said: ‘It is my staff. I lean upon it, and with it, I beat down leaves (making them fall) upon my sheep. And I have other uses for it.’"
  20,19,He said: ‘Throw it down Musa (Moses).’
  20,20,"So he threw it down. And behold, it was a snake moving fast."
  20,21,He said: ‘Pick it up and do not fear. We shall restore it to its original state.
  20,22,Now enclose your hand to your armpit. It will emerge (shining) white without any blemish. (This is yet) another sign.
  20,23,(We are doing this) so that We can show you some of Our greater signs.
  20,24,Go to Pharaoh. He has indeed transgressed all bounds.’
  20,25,He said: ‘My Lord! Expand my breast for me.
  20,26,And make my task easy for me.
  20,27,"And remove the hitch from my tongue (granting me clarity of speech),"
  20,28,so that people may understand my discourse (easily).
  20,29,"And appoint for me a minister from my family,"
  20,30,my brother Harun (Aaron).
  20,31,"Increase my strength through him,"
  20,32,and make him my associate in my task.
  20,33,"So that we may glorify You much,"
  20,34,and remember You much.
  20,35,"Indeed, You are always watching over us.’"
  20,36,He said: ‘Musa (Moses)! Your request has been granted.
  20,37,"And indeed, We had shown you favour before,"
